      "data": {
        "body": "Run a reversible rendering experiment: clicking an internal graph portal opens its target alongside, binds the graph-local portal to the resolved target surface in workspace state, and presents one shared surface in the bridge gap. This is a hypothesis to inspect, not a settled semantic law.",
        "priority": "critical",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "targetDate": "",
        "successMetrics": [
          "Portal activation adds or reuses the target graph in the workspace without replacing the current document.",
          "The experiment records a workspace-only portal-to-surface binding and does not mutate either graph.",
          "A shared projection appears in the compatible bridge gap and identifies both graph-local participants.",
          "Closing the target restores the separate portal presentation.",
          "Visual inspection determines whether shared identity is a useful model before the contract is promoted."
        ],
