      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Experimental status\n\nThis graph records an attempted solution, not a normative contract. The working hypothesis is that a graph-local portal and the live target surface it resolves may be presented as one workspace boundary node while retaining different graph-local IDs.\n\nPromote this to a contract only after visual inspection confirms that navigation, edges, frame boundaries, closing, duplicate targets, and named surfaces remain understandable. Roll back the workspace binding and shared projection if the result obscures graph ownership or semantic identity.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
