      "data": {
        "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" viewBox=\"0 0 920 460\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A local edge to a portal is rendered through a bridge aperture to the same identity's live representation when the target graph is connected\"><rect width=\"920\" height=\"460\" rx=\"24\" fill=\"#161326\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"42\" fill=\"#f5f2ff\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\">SAME ENDPOINT · DIFFERENT REPRESENTATION</text><g fill=\"#202238\" stroke=\"#778096\" stroke-width=\"3\"><path d=\"M42 72 H430 V202 M430 266 V390 H42 Z\"/><path d=\"M550 72 H878 V390 H550 V266 M550 202 V72\"/></g><text x=\"66\" y=\"106\" fill=\"#e8e5f0\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\">Graph A · owns the edge</text><text x=\"574\" y=\"106\" fill=\"#e8e5f0\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\">Graph B · spatially present</text><rect x=\"78\" y=\"210\" width=\"126\" height=\"62\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"#26354a\" stroke=\"#77a7ff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"141\" y=\"247\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Local node</text><rect x=\"278\" y=\"194\" width=\"132\" height=\"94\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#392d4d\" stroke=\"#b27cff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"344\" y=\"226\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Portal</text><text x=\"344\" y=\"248\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#d7c4f5\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">represents X</text><text x=\"344\" y=\"268\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#d7c4f5\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">saved endpoint</text><rect x=\"586\" y=\"194\" width=\"156\" height=\"94\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#203744\" stroke=\"#5de1ff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"664\" y=\"226\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Live representation</text><text x=\"664\" y=\"248\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#a6edf7\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">represents X</text><text x=\"664\" y=\"268\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#a6edf7\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"10\">workspace endpoint</text><path d=\"M204 241 H278\" stroke=\"#77a7ff\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><path d=\"M410 241 H430\" stroke=\"#b27cff\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><path d=\"M430 241 H550\" stroke=\"#5de1ff\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-dasharray=\"12 8\"/><path d=\"M550 241 H586\" stroke=\"#5de1ff\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><path d=\"M489 223 L503 241 L489 259\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5de1ff\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"490\" y=\"307\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#d8d1e7\" font-family=\"monospace\" font-size=\"11\">bridge-authorized presentation continuation</text><rect x=\"88\" y=\"336\" width=\"744\" height=\"34\" rx=\"17\" fill=\"#242039\" stroke=\"#81729e\"/><text x=\"460\" y=\"358\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#eee8ff\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\">Disconnect: live representation disappears; the edge renders to the portal again.</text><text x=\"460\" y=\"424\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#bfb5d2\" font-family=\"system-ui\" font-size=\"11\">No retarget · no remote edge · no document mutation · no undo entry</text></svg>",
        "altText": "Graph A owns a local edge ending at a portal representing identity X. When Graph B is connected, the same edge is visually continued through a bridge aperture to a live representation of identity X. Disconnecting returns the rendering to the portal without mutation.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-bridge-apertures-declaration"
        },
        "memo": "The portal remains the saved endpoint. The live target is an identity-equivalent workspace representative, and the bridge supplies only crossing authority and aperture geometry."
      },
      "style": {
        "background": "#111321",
        "borderColor": "#4f466f",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 20
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "workspace-bridge-apertures-acceptance-contract",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Bridge Aperture Acceptance Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 1160,
        "y": -360
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 500,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Identity-Preserving Connection Acceptance Contract\n\n## Authored graph integrity\n\n- Every saved edge retains its graph-local source, target, handles, label, type, and identity through connection changes.\n- A remote relationship endpoint is represented by a local portal or graph-backed projection.\n- The remote graph receives no mirrored edge merely because it becomes spatially present.\n- A bridge is an authored authority and geometry source, not a semantic endpoint substitute.\n\n## Identity integrity\n\n- Portal and live replacement share one canonical represented identity.\n- Graph-root, exposed-port, and node-specific portal targets remain distinguishable.\n- Presentation payload and surface selection cannot silently change the represented node.\n- Ambiguous identity or duplicate target instances require explicit resolution and never use nearest-frame guessing.\n\n## Rendering integrity\n\n- Target absent: the edge terminates visibly on the local portal.\n- Target present and bridge compatible: the same edge renders through an aperture to the live representative.\n- Target closed or disconnected: rendering returns to the portal without graph mutation.\n- Dormant bridges and independently opened unrelated graphs create no apertures or corridors.\n- Main workspace and minimap consume one resolved presentation model.\n\n## Validation integrity\n\n- The task-planning class bridges in the reported planning graph remain Legend-only.\n- Connect, disconnect, restore, collapse, and foldout preserve graph signatures and dirty state.\n- Root, named-port, node-specific, missing-target, ambiguous-target, and duplicate-instance cases are covered.\n- Focused tests, production build, and real-browser smoke results remain honest."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-bridge-apertures-declaration"
        },
        "markdown": "# Identity-Preserving Connection Acceptance Contract\n\n## Authored graph integrity\n\n- Every saved edge retains its graph-local source, target, handles, label, type, and identity through connection changes.\n- A remote relationship endpoint is represented by a local portal or graph-backed projection.\n- The remote graph receives no mirrored edge merely because it becomes spatially present.\n- A bridge is an authored authority and geometry source, not a semantic endpoint substitute.\n\n## Identity integrity\n\n- Portal and live replacement share one canonical represented identity.\n- Graph-root, exposed-port, and node-specific portal targets remain distinguishable.\n- Presentation payload and surface selection cannot silently change the represented node.\n- Ambiguous identity or duplicate target instances require explicit resolution and never use nearest-frame guessing.\n\n## Rendering integrity\n\n- Target absent: the edge terminates visibly on the local portal.\n- Target present and bridge compatible: the same edge renders through an aperture to the live representative.\n- Target closed or disconnected: rendering returns to the portal without graph mutation.\n- Dormant bridges and independently opened unrelated graphs create no apertures or corridors.\n- Main workspace and minimap consume one resolved presentation model.\n\n## Validation integrity\n\n- The task-planning class bridges in the reported planning graph remain Legend-only.\n- Connect, disconnect, restore, collapse, and foldout preserve graph signatures and dirty state.\n- Root, named-port, node-specific, missing-target, ambiguous-target, and duplicate-instance cases are covered.\n- Focused tests, production build, and real-browser smoke results remain honest."
      }
    }
